mcp-computer-use
================

This product depends on `BackgroundComputerUseKit`
(https://github.com/actuallyepic/background-computer-use), MIT-licensed,
© cam + anupam (dubdubdub labs). Pinned to commit
`dcf55a3feee557ebdcda4afa6241c82dc6abdd8c`. The Swift wrapper at
native/macos/Sources/McpComputerUseHelper/ imports the kit via SwiftPM
and translates upstream's API into this project's existing JSON-over-stdio
wire protocol; see UPSTREAM_SYNC.md for the upgrade ritual.

The Node-side TypeScript (src/native/macos-bridge.ts) is owned by this
project, tailored to the MCP server lifecycle and safety model.

Historical note: prior releases (v0.1.x) shipped a vendored Swift helper
seeded from injaneity/pi-computer-use commit 96434a7 (MIT © Zane Chee).
That file was deleted in v0.2.0 when the helper internals were swapped to
BackgroundComputerUseKit. Git history preserves the original for archeology.

